# RONDB-1124: a second pure EndOfData after the one that ends a join
# aggregation (testJoinAggNdbApi Test 26).  DBTC sends it when an API
# close crosses the end of the scan ("Confirming scan close"); DBTC
# error insert 8320 sends the final EndOfData twice.  Each query read to
# the end must give the right result, each query closed at once must
# close, and the cluster must stay up.  Before the fix a debug NDB API
# aborted on assert(m_finalWorkers < getWorkerCount()) in
# NdbQueryImpl::setFetchTerminated(), or on assert(m_scanningQuery) in
# NdbTransaction::receiveSCAN_TABCONF().  Debug only: the error insert
# needs debug data nodes.
#
# A debug NDB API may log a dropped EndOfData with a timestamp, so the
# program's output goes to a file and only its result lines are
# compared.  A crash fails the --exec; a failed check prints a FAILED
# line and "Some tests FAILED", which differ from the result file.
--source include/have_ndb.inc
--source include/have_ndb_debug.inc

--let $dup_eod_out = $MYSQLTEST_VARDIR/tmp/testJoinAggNdbApiDupEndOfData.out
--echo Running testJoinAggNdbApi --only 26
--error 0,1
--exec $NDB_PUSH_AGG_DIR/testJoinAggNdbApi -c "$NDB_CONNECTSTRING" -m $MASTER_MYPORT --only 26 > $dup_eod_out 2>&1
--exec grep -E "^(Test 26|FAILED|All tests|Some tests)" $dup_eod_out
--remove_file $dup_eod_out

# The program clears 8320, but not if it died: clear it here too.
--exec $NDB_MGM -e "all error 0" >> $NDB_TOOLS_OUTPUT

# Clean up database created by test program
DROP DATABASE IF EXISTS test_db;
